{"id": "underground_fire_hydrant", "name": "Underground fire hydrant", "description": "Below-ground hydrant of the UK pattern (BS 750): a screw-down hydrant on a branch from the fire main, in a chamber under a hinged cast iron surface box set flush with the ground. The origin is the top of the cover at ground level. Defaults: DN80 inlet, one 65 mm screwed outlet, main about 0.9 m below ground. Mark it with a hydrant indicator plate.", "tags": ["underground hydrant", "hydrant chamber", "hydrant pit", "hydrant", "fire main", "firefighting", "suppression", "fire", "outdoor", "foundations"], "ifc_class": "IfcFireSuppressionTerminal", "predefined_type": "FIREHYDRANT", "params": {"depth": [0.9, 0.75, 1.5, "m", "ground level to underside of chamber"], "main": [0.1, 0.08, 0.15, "m", "branch pipe diameter"]}, "geometry": [{"shape": "extrude", "at": [0, 0, 0.1], "material": "concrete", "profile": {"points": [[-0.4, -0.3], [0.4, -0.3], [0.4, 0.3], [-0.4, 0.3]], "holes": [[[-0.28, -0.18], [0.28, -0.18], [0.28, 0.18], [-0.28, 0.18]]]}, "height": "depth - 0.2"}, {"shape": "box", "at": ["(0) - (0.8) / 2", "(0) - (0.6) / 2", 0], "material": "concrete", "size": [0.8, 0.6, 0.1]}, {"shape": "extrude", "at": [0, 0, "depth - 0.1"], "material": "iron", "profile": {"points": [[-0.29, -0.2], [0.29, -0.2], [0.29, 0.2], [-0.29, 0.2]], "holes": [[[-0.22, -0.13], [0.22, -0.13], [0.22, 0.13], [-0.22, 0.13]]]}, "height": 0.1}, {"shape": "box", "at": ["(0) - (0.43) / 2", "(0) - (0.25) / 2", "depth - 0.03"], "material": "yellow", "size": [0.43, 0.25, 0.03]}, {"shape": "cylinder", "at": [-0.4, 0, "0.1 + main"], "rotate": [0, 90, 0], "material": "iron", "radius": "main / 2", "height": 0.4}, {"shape": "cylinder", "at": [0, 0, "0.1 + main / 2"], "material": "red", "radius": 0.075, "height": "depth - 0.45 - main"}, {"shape": "cylinder", "at": [0, 0, "depth - 0.35"], "material": "red", "radius": 0.11, "height": 0.025}, {"shape": "cylinder", "at": [0.06, 0, "depth - 0.325"], "material": "brass", "radius"